{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979708225,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8bfdcbffe5O38dMU7vIoenG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xSSIZyHR38Zf0qHm2FMGDgvZ","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**CL term:**\\n- [CL_0002423](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002423) — DN2a thymocyte\\n- [CL_0002424](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002424) — DN2b thymocyte\\n\\nFor both DN2a and DN2b:\\n[x] in taxon: Mus musculus\\n[ ] never in taxon\\n[ ] present in taxon\\n\\n**Rationale**\\nDN2a and DN2b are defined based on c-Kit (CD117) expression levels (Kit-high vs Kit-low), following the classical DN1–DN4 (CD44/CD25) staging system. This staging system is validated only in mouse thymopoiesis.\\nHuman thymocyte development does not utilize DN2a or DN2b nomenclature, and Kit-high/Kit-low DN2 subsets are not reproducibly defined in human thymus. The Cell Ontology comment for DN2a explicitly states: “Observed in mice… molecular markers characterizing double negative thymocytes are different across species.”\\nTherefore, these terms should receive an explicit “in taxon: Mus musculus” constraint. The absence of a taxon annotation (and the presence of human_subset tags) is currently misleading.\\n\\n**References:**\\nPMID: 25060579 — Review of mouse DN1–DN4 staging; DN2a/DN2b defined via Kit-high/Kit-low only in mouse.\\nPMID: 20543111 — Experimental definition of DN2a (Kit-high) and DN2b (Kit-low) in adult mouse thymus.\\nPMID: 32079746 — Human thymus single-cell atlas; DN2a/DN2b subsets not observed or defined in human development.\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"[Taxon constraint] Add taxon constraints to DN2a (CL_0002423) and DN2b (CL_0002424)\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3500\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**CL term:**\\n- [CL_0002423](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002423) — DN2a thymocyte\\n- [CL_0002424](http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CL_0002424) — DN2b thymocyte\\n\\nFor both DN2a and DN2b:\\n[x] in taxon: Mus musculus\\n[ ] never in taxon\\n[ ] present in taxon\\n\\n**Rationale**\\nDN2a and DN2b are defined based on c-Kit (CD117) expression levels (Kit-high vs Kit-low), following the classical DN1–DN4 (CD44/CD25) staging system. This staging system is validated only in mouse thymopoiesis.\\nHuman thymocyte development does not utilize DN2a or DN2b nomenclature, and Kit-high/Kit-low DN2 subsets are not reproducibly defined in human thymus. The Cell Ontology comment for DN2a explicitly states: “Observed in mice… molecular markers characterizing double negative thymocytes are different across species.”\\nTherefore, these terms should receive an explicit “in taxon: Mus musculus” constraint. The absence of a taxon annotation (and the presence of human_subset tags) is currently misleading.\\n\\n**References:**\\nPMID: 25060579 — Review of mouse DN1–DN4 staging; DN2a/DN2b defined via Kit-high/Kit-low only in mouse.\\nPMID: 20543111 — Experimental definition of DN2a (Kit-high) and DN2b (Kit-low) in adult mouse thymus.\\nPMID: 32079746 — Human thymus single-cell atlas; DN2a/DN2b subsets not observed or defined in human development.\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"[Taxon constraint] Add taxon constraints to DN2a (CL_0002423) and DN2b (CL_0002424)\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3500\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778979708186,"end":1778979708222}},"id":"prt_e33741d0c001oYnJ4cKzog0amk","sessionID":"ses_1cc8bfdcbffe5O38dMU7vIoenG","messageID":"msg_e33740359001rvISeNloWoiUwm"}}
