{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979801734,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8bfdcbffe5O38dMU7vIoenG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_kpzhy7i0w0pUBADTqykFmJLE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added explicit `in taxon: Mus musculus` constraints to `DN2a thymocyte` (`CL_0002423`) and `DN2b thymocyte` (`CL_0002424`) to align the ontology with the existing term comments and mouse-specific staging usage described in the issue.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the requested taxon constraints for the two DN2 thymocyte subset terms discussed in issue #3500.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+- Added `SubClassOf(... ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))` to `CL_0002423` (DN2a thymocyte).\n+- Added `SubClassOf(... ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_10090))` to `CL_0002424` (DN2b thymocyte).\n+- Annotated both new taxon axioms with the issue URL using `IAO:0000233`, following existing curation patterns in `cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+Rationale:\n+- The issue body describes DN2a and DN2b as mouse-specific subdivisions based on Kit-high versus Kit-low expression in the classical DN1-DN4 staging framework.\n+- Both terms already carried comments stating they are observed in mice and warning that equivalent double-negative thymocyte marker schemes differ across species, especially between mouse and human.\n+- Adding explicit `in taxon` restrictions makes that species scope machine-readable and removes the ambiguity noted in the issue.\n+\n+Validation and review performed:\n+- Inspected the existing term stanzas for `CL_0002423` and `CL_0002424` in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+- Checked nearby and global examples of existing `in taxon` assertions to match file style.\n+- Ran `robot convert --input src/ontology/cl-edit.owl --output /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-issue3500.owl`